      "notes": "The one People writer, both modes (ruled 2026-09-02): PATCH /v0/{base}/{People} with {performUpsert: {fieldsToMergeOn: [\"Contact Key\"]}, records (ten per request), typecast: true}, 200 ms apart, so 50 rows per second against the Airtable node's measured 4.5. No retry: a 429 locks the base for 30 s; a request that is not 2xx counts every record in it as a write error with the reason and the pass continues. Written rows are counted from the answer's records[], never from item ids."
